WEBVTT

00:10.120 --> 00:12.060
Who is he? Where?

00:13.350 --> 00:15.180
Which one? That guy?

00:17.010 --> 00:22.810
For Lost Love

00:17.020 --> 00:20.550
Oh, him? The one lying
facedown on the table?

00:20.980 --> 00:23.970
That's right. That youngster.

00:23.970 --> 00:26.230
Okay, okay. I see.

00:26.230 --> 00:28.830
He looks like someone who'd do that.

00:29.790 --> 00:32.000
He's the guy who lost to a pig.

00:33.150 --> 00:35.870
Guys like him really do exist.

00:35.870 --> 00:40.280
I'm amazed he had the balls to say
he wanted to join the king's guard.

00:42.160 --> 00:43.790
So, what did you want?

00:43.790 --> 00:47.410
All we have to do is
tell him he's been rejected?

00:47.410 --> 00:50.050
That's right. All you need to do
is convey the message.

00:51.560 --> 00:53.420
Fine, I guess.

00:54.420 --> 00:55.430
Aw, damn.

00:56.030 --> 00:59.190
I'm not sure I can keep myself
from doing more.

01:00.300 --> 01:01.810
You want to mock him?

01:02.240 --> 01:04.800
I mean, just look at his stupid face.

01:08.230 --> 01:11.850
Go on. I'll buy you drinks later.

01:11.850 --> 01:13.150
Okay.

01:13.710 --> 01:15.220
Quit laughing so much.

01:15.220 --> 01:16.740
Yeah, but...

01:33.960 --> 01:37.980
You lot look just as stupid as he does.

03:17.160 --> 03:18.560
Olmar?

03:20.800 --> 03:23.870
Olmar, do you have a minute?

03:29.500 --> 03:31.570
My name is Brodd.

03:31.570 --> 03:33.830
I'm a member of the king's guard.

03:36.230 --> 03:37.420
And?

03:37.810 --> 03:43.430
I've brought a message from Wulf,
captain of His Majesty's guard.

03:43.690 --> 03:45.580
You're here to tell me I've been rejected.

03:46.390 --> 03:49.610
Now, now. I'm here on a job.

03:49.610 --> 03:51.920
Allow me to deliver my message.

03:55.990 --> 04:02.380
Olmar, regarding your request
to join the king's guard,

04:02.770 --> 04:05.790
the captain spoke highly
of your determination

04:05.790 --> 04:09.830
to offer your life in service of His Majesty.

04:11.390 --> 04:16.590
However, upon seeing your skill with a sword,

04:17.390 --> 04:20.580
he remarked that your skills
"need improvement."

04:23.080 --> 04:27.960
Therefore, we regret to inform you that...

04:29.220 --> 04:32.510
Regret to inform you that...

04:42.700 --> 04:46.870
Th-There's nothing regrettable about it.
You lost to a pig!

04:49.080 --> 04:51.650
Don't say that.

04:51.650 --> 04:53.280
I-I can't breathe.

04:54.750 --> 04:58.940
I heard... I heard you
couldn't even cut a pig.

04:58.940 --> 05:04.130
Why not? Was the pig wearing
chain mail? A hauberk perhaps?

05:04.580 --> 05:07.920
Oh, but on a pig,
I guess you'd call it a hogberk.

05:16.910 --> 05:20.650
Forgive me. I shouldn't laugh.

05:21.140 --> 05:24.360
He failed to get a job.

05:24.360 --> 05:28.030
Do you guys know anyone who's hiring?

05:28.630 --> 05:32.660
Come to think of it,
the castle was looking for a new cook.

05:33.010 --> 05:36.300
That won't work. He can't chop up pigs!

05:45.930 --> 05:47.180
I'm dying!

06:01.160 --> 06:05.070
A warrior answers insults with his sword!

06:05.500 --> 06:06.760
Draw your weapon!

06:13.730 --> 06:16.050
But you couldn't even cut a pig.

06:16.650 --> 06:19.550
I'm dying! I'm gonna die laughing!

06:22.130 --> 06:22.630
Whoa!

06:23.480 --> 06:25.120
What's your problem?

06:25.560 --> 06:29.400
You'll hurt someone doing that, you weakling.

06:35.280 --> 06:36.510
Come on, let's go.

06:36.510 --> 06:37.300
Wait for me.

06:37.300 --> 06:38.390
It's a fight!

06:38.390 --> 06:40.650
There's a five-on-one
happening by the stalls!

06:40.950 --> 06:42.540
They've got swords!

06:42.540 --> 06:45.070
Someone's gonna bleed!

06:46.050 --> 06:46.810
Get him!

06:46.810 --> 06:48.160
Kill him!

06:48.430 --> 06:50.340
You've got this, young one!

06:50.340 --> 06:52.050
I'll take him on myself.

06:52.050 --> 06:56.660
We'd dishonor ourselves as warriors if we
ganged up on a guy who can't even cut a pig.

06:57.710 --> 06:58.960
You'd better not lose.

07:00.660 --> 07:03.860
Look at you, all excited to fight.

07:05.050 --> 07:08.750
I'll help you train, Olmar.

07:15.660 --> 07:18.060
Come on, stand up. You can do it.

07:27.580 --> 07:30.600
He's as pathetic as I was told.

07:51.920 --> 07:53.480
Stand up, Olmar.

07:54.240 --> 07:56.560
Don't lie on the ground during a duel.

08:03.070 --> 08:04.160
Thorgil...

08:06.070 --> 08:10.840
Thorgil, they... they humiliated me.

08:11.830 --> 08:13.420
I know. I can see that.

08:13.920 --> 08:16.540
Get back on your feet and kill him.

08:26.550 --> 08:27.480
Stand up.

08:35.740 --> 08:37.940
Stand up, Olmar!

08:45.750 --> 08:48.660
Th-Thorgil, I...

08:49.390 --> 08:50.980
Listen to me, Olmar.

08:51.580 --> 08:54.870
There are only two options for a
warrior who has been insulted.

08:55.580 --> 08:57.560
Kill or die.

08:58.100 --> 09:00.000
If you can't kill him, then you'll die here.

09:02.600 --> 09:07.860
I won't allow you to go on living
without addressing this insult.

09:09.440 --> 09:11.540
Fight and become a man.

09:12.110 --> 09:14.430
Today is the day.

09:15.780 --> 09:16.890
Thor...

09:16.890 --> 09:17.910
Go on.

09:21.990 --> 09:23.390
What the hell was that?

09:24.870 --> 09:26.950
Imagine it, Olmar.

09:26.950 --> 09:29.780
Imagine the moment you
cut off your enemy's head.

09:29.780 --> 09:31.780
Y-Yeah...

09:32.260 --> 09:35.080
Let me hear you. Say it from your stomach.

09:35.910 --> 09:36.780
Yeah.

09:36.780 --> 09:37.750
Louder.

09:37.750 --> 09:38.780
Yeah!

09:39.430 --> 09:40.890
Imagine it.

09:40.890 --> 09:45.040
Imagine your enemy crying with remorse in a
pool of blood with his guts strewn about him.

09:45.370 --> 09:46.670
Yeah!

09:46.980 --> 09:49.170
Show some spirit, Olmar!

09:49.170 --> 09:50.380
Yeah!

09:50.380 --> 09:53.050
Kill the bastard! Kill him!

09:53.050 --> 09:53.990
Yeah!

09:53.990 --> 09:56.030
Go!

09:59.690 --> 10:03.640
Uh-oh. Provoke him, and all of
a sudden, he's raring to go.

10:08.070 --> 10:10.720
The time for practice is over.

10:48.780 --> 10:49.780
Seriously?

10:51.110 --> 10:51.870
Hey!

10:52.400 --> 10:53.730
You bastard!

10:54.220 --> 10:55.850
Don't let him escape alive.

10:55.850 --> 10:58.470
We'll reclaim our honor here and now.

10:58.470 --> 10:59.370
Yeah.

11:00.790 --> 11:04.740
Well done, Olmar. That's my little brother.

11:07.870 --> 11:09.590
Leave the rest to me.

11:26.560 --> 11:28.390
He's dead...

11:30.920 --> 11:32.360
Did I kill him?

11:53.790 --> 11:56.980
I killed a man...

12:16.360 --> 12:17.300
So it was his eye.

12:18.700 --> 12:21.150
It was damaged by a rock or something.

12:23.430 --> 12:25.410
Olmar! Thorgil!

12:25.950 --> 12:28.300
Move. Get out of the way.

12:33.710 --> 12:37.360
Wh-Wh-What is this?

12:38.420 --> 12:39.760
What happened?

12:43.350 --> 12:44.550
Y-You...

12:50.470 --> 12:52.440
Calm down, Dad.

12:53.070 --> 12:55.690
Calm down? You want me to calm down?

12:55.950 --> 12:59.800
You... You killed the king's men!

13:00.240 --> 13:03.410
What are you going to do about this?

13:03.860 --> 13:05.660
We did nothing wrong.

13:05.910 --> 13:06.980
What?

13:06.980 --> 13:09.620
Olmar was insulted, so he fought a duel.

13:09.620 --> 13:10.990
He defended his honor.

13:10.990 --> 13:11.910
But...

13:12.210 --> 13:13.670
There were five of them.

13:13.670 --> 13:17.250
No one could object to me joining the fight.

13:17.820 --> 13:20.480
You're his father.
You should be praising him.

13:24.540 --> 13:27.640
Duels are forbidden by law!

13:28.100 --> 13:31.520
Nobody cares about that law.

13:31.980 --> 13:38.400
They had swords. They must've known
insulting him would be costly.

13:39.340 --> 13:41.630
They knew that, and insulted him regardless.

13:41.630 --> 13:44.400
The churls deserved to die.

13:47.930 --> 13:50.240
Move. Clear the way.

13:49.660 --> 13:50.910
Hey, what's going on?

13:51.650 --> 13:53.470
It's... It's the guards.

13:53.470 --> 13:57.020
We did nothing wrong.
Duels happen all the time.

13:57.020 --> 13:59.140
Normally we wouldn't be punished.

14:03.510 --> 14:09.120
Who dared to start a commotion
just outside His Majesty's castle?

14:10.620 --> 14:13.480
Step forward and present yourselves.

14:16.060 --> 14:19.310
What's going on here? Olmar is alive.

14:19.820 --> 14:23.130
Ketil's here, too. Who's the other one?

14:23.130 --> 14:26.960
I don't know. Probably a family member.

14:29.000 --> 14:32.940
I am Thorgil, son of Ketil,
member of the king's guard.

14:33.370 --> 14:36.310
This is my father, Ketil,
and my younger brother, Olmar.

14:37.120 --> 14:38.830
This was a fair duel.

14:39.560 --> 14:41.390
We have done nothing wrong.

14:42.500 --> 14:46.590
Silence. The king has forbidden duels.

14:48.440 --> 14:54.280
You've disrespected the king.
You're all under arrest.

14:55.130 --> 14:56.940
I-I knew it.

14:56.940 --> 14:59.760
See? I told you so, Thorgil!

15:05.260 --> 15:06.900
Come on, hands behind your back.

15:06.900 --> 15:07.950
Stop resisting.

15:08.330 --> 15:10.910
W-W-Wait a minute. I didn't—

15:12.190 --> 15:14.840
Hand over your sword and
put your hands behind your back.

15:17.180 --> 15:18.830
Hey, are you deaf?

15:31.260 --> 15:32.400
What?

15:33.950 --> 15:36.020
You... You asshole!

16:08.510 --> 16:10.010
Bastard!

16:24.190 --> 16:27.400
H-Have you actually lost
your mind this time, Thorgil?

16:27.780 --> 16:30.900
It's over. There's no coming back from this.

16:34.550 --> 16:37.910
There's something I want to ask you.

16:39.870 --> 16:43.940
I'm not a patient man.
Be careful how you answer my question.

16:44.580 --> 16:46.160
If you tell me, I'll spare your life.

16:48.080 --> 16:50.390
Why did you allow Olmar to win?

16:51.560 --> 16:52.230
What?

16:52.940 --> 16:55.110
They... let me win?

16:56.100 --> 16:57.080
Tell me.

16:57.080 --> 16:58.560
I-I don't know—

17:06.820 --> 17:08.780
You should heed people's warnings.

17:09.910 --> 17:13.360
Tell me. Why did you set up Olmar?

17:15.900 --> 17:22.380
To... To arrest Ketil.

17:23.460 --> 17:31.300
We had Olmar kill the king's men
so Ketil would be held responsible

17:32.110 --> 17:35.100
for his son's disrespect to the king.

17:38.540 --> 17:42.620
Wh-What did I do to deserve that?

17:43.820 --> 17:48.520
I-I simply followed Captain Wulf's orders.

17:49.320 --> 17:51.900
Please, let me tend to my wounds.

17:52.180 --> 17:56.110
The blood... It won't stop!

17:57.760 --> 18:01.420
It's over. King Canute
has set his sights on us.

18:05.380 --> 18:07.190
No, Dad.

18:09.360 --> 18:10.670
Thorgil...

18:12.060 --> 18:14.420
This is the beginning.

18:15.100 --> 18:17.080
Our enemy is strong.

18:38.900 --> 18:43.030
I see. So Ketil's family escaped.

18:43.640 --> 18:46.460
I'm sorry, Your Majesty.

18:47.520 --> 18:51.270
I sent men to secure their ships and
lodgings, but they haven't been found.

18:51.980 --> 18:53.710
We're currently searching for them.

18:54.380 --> 18:58.600
It's my fault that we failed to capture Thorgil.

19:00.560 --> 19:02.850
He sounds like a skilled warrior.

19:03.350 --> 19:05.620
Yes. He was a good subordinate.

19:07.480 --> 19:09.200
It doesn't affect our plans.

19:09.690 --> 19:12.180
We have our excuse to punish them.

19:12.810 --> 19:15.730
As planned, we'll head to Ketil's farm.

19:16.710 --> 19:19.200
If Ketil isn't there, then that's fine.

19:19.620 --> 19:23.450
If he is and resists us,
then we'll simply overwhelm him.

19:23.450 --> 19:28.400
Yes, Your Majesty.
I'll mobilize 32 of your guard.

19:29.180 --> 19:34.630
With 70 of Floki's Jomsvikings,
we'll have 102 men altogether.

19:35.560 --> 19:39.020
That should be enough.
When will Floki arrive?

19:39.670 --> 19:42.230
Within three days, from Jomsborg.

19:44.180 --> 19:47.560
Then we'll leave at dawn three days from now.

19:48.350 --> 19:49.110
Leave me.

19:49.850 --> 19:50.600
Yes, Your Majesty.

20:16.000 --> 20:18.910
What are you laughing about, King Sweyn?

20:20.040 --> 20:22.390
Don't be so angry.

20:22.810 --> 20:30.280
Why shouldn't a father be pleased
his son is beginning to resemble himself?

20:37.200 --> 20:39.400
Keep going.

20:40.750 --> 20:48.340
You'll need to pile up plenty of
bodies to reach the top.

21:03.910 --> 21:09.190
All right, gentlemen. You can come out now.

21:15.200 --> 21:17.190
These barrels reek of salt.

21:19.120 --> 21:23.750
You saved us, Leif.
I appreciate your kindness.

21:24.350 --> 21:26.860
This isn't an act of kindness. It's a deal.

21:27.400 --> 21:29.950
Don't forget the promise you made me.

21:30.520 --> 21:35.960
I wouldn't smuggle criminals
out of mere kindness.

21:31.840 --> 21:33.260
Boy, that stinks.

21:36.290 --> 21:40.600
Do you have any idea how difficult
it was to convince my men?

21:41.830 --> 21:45.260
Don't worry. A warrior
never goes back on his word.

21:45.830 --> 21:51.390
Ketil's farm will buy all your
cargo for triple its value.

21:52.350 --> 21:54.440
Don't forget about Thorfinn, too.

21:54.790 --> 21:58.230
Of course. You can have the slave, too.

21:58.880 --> 22:00.570
Right, Dad?

22:04.760 --> 22:06.950
Dad, you can come out now.

22:06.950 --> 22:08.850
Shut up!

22:08.850 --> 22:12.450
Don't talk to me. Leave me alone.

22:13.120 --> 22:15.040
He's in a bad mood.

22:15.790 --> 22:18.870
Don't forget our promise.

22:51.040 --> 22:54.190
All right. That's enough for today.

22:54.740 --> 22:56.900
Yeah.

22:56.900 --> 22:58.320
Good work today.

23:13.600 --> 23:15.020
What's the matter, Thorfinn?

23:15.790 --> 23:18.060
Is the sunset that captivating?

23:22.000 --> 23:22.870
No...

23:29.380 --> 23:31.680
Mock me if you wish.

23:32.980 --> 23:35.270
Curse me if you must.

23:37.500 --> 23:41.000
I do all of this to create my utopia.

23:45.990 --> 23:50.500
All for lost love.

25:36.700 --> 25:40.080
Dark Clouds

25:38.020 --> 25:39.230
"Dark Clouds."
